# Shorebird Update Management Plan

This plan documents how to manage Over-The-Air (OTA) updates using Shorebird, specifically addressing automatic vs. manual update logic and the necessary CLI commands.

## Overview
The project currently uses [SmartUpdateManager](file:///d:/saas/ramadan_assistant/lib/core/utils/smart_update_manager.dart#13-348) which integrates with Shorebird and Firebase Remote Config to manage three types of update tracks:
1.  **auto-update**: Patches that are downloaded and installed automatically in the background on app start.
2.  **manual-update**: Patches that require user confirmation via a dialog.
3.  **critical-update**: Patches that force the user to update and restart.

## Shorebird CLI Commands

### 1. Initial Release
To create the base version that can receive patches, use:
```bash
shorebird release android --artifact apk '--' --no-tree-shake-icons
```
> [!NOTE]
> Releasing an APK allows Shorebird to track the version. Future patches will be applied to this base version.

### 2. Creating a Patch (The Update)
To send an update to users, use the `patch` command instead of `release`.

#### For Automatic Updates
The current code in [main.dart](file:///d:/saas/ramadan_assistant/lib/main.dart) checks the `auto-update` track. To push a patch that installs automatically:
```bash
shorebird patch android --track auto-update
```

#### For Manual/Default Updates
To push a patch to the default track (which triggers a dialog if configured):
```bash
shorebird patch android --track manual-update
```

## Update Logic Control

### How to make a patch "Auto"
The code in [main.dart](file:///d:/saas/ramadan_assistant/lib/main.dart) (Line 75) already calls `updateManager.checkAutoUpdates()`. 
Any patch pushed to the `auto-update` track via the CLI will be downloaded automatically when the user starts the app.

### How to Disable Auto Update
If you want to stop automatic updates, you have two options:

1.  **Code Change**: Remove or comment out the auto-check in [lib/main.dart](file:///d:/saas/ramadan_assistant/lib/main.dart):
    ```dart
    // In main.dart
    // updateManager.checkAutoUpdates(); // Remove this to disable auto-check
    ```
2.  **Track Management**: Only push patches to the `manual-update` or default track. Patches on these tracks will not be downloaded by the [checkAutoUpdates()](file:///d:/saas/ramadan_assistant/lib/core/utils/smart_update_manager.dart#126-164) call unless the logic is changed.

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
1.  **Auto Update**:
    -   Push a patch using `shorebird patch android --track auto-update`.
    -   Open the app.
    -   Check logs (via `adb logcat` or VS Code console) to see `📥 Auto update available, downloading...`.
    -   Restart the app to see the patch applied.
2.  **Manual Update**:
    -   Push a patch using `shorebird patch android --track manual-update`.
    -   Navigate to the settings or wherever manual update check is triggered.
    -   Verify the update dialog appears.
